-- aar/w3/aar_row_578_draft1.sql. DRAFT 1 by W3 (session_01H1X3ANsGiMnhnbkfphocmo) for W1's grade, then the coordinator (seat 36). NOT RUN by W3.
-- One ask_aar_snapshots row for ASK 578 and its ask_aar_builders row.
-- Every value is from the Wall post named in its source (read by W3 in this turn: 11739 to 11753 heads, 11837, 11842, 11844, 11848, 11850, 11851, 11852 whole; 11148 to 11175 heads), from W4's files under /mnt/project-files/ask578/w4/ (md5sum and sha256sum by W3, 19:2x CST 2026-11-24; notes578.md, out_t578c.txt and write578_run.txt read; the Library Check node and the readers read in fetchback_child_578.json), from audit_log row 41852 (read by W3), from md_notes_rulings row 539, or from W4's thread note to W3 of 19:09 CST (the write card).
-- NOT READ by W3: the write card and the C7 test card themselves (W4's thread); W1's grade and readback files in git (the Wall posts name them); n8n.
-- HASH KINDS: W4 and W1 name the targets by sha256 prefixes (engine c5bc9fd3, child 7eb149f4). md5_written holds the md5 of the two target files as W3 computed them; each build_files element gives both. W1: confirm the two md5 values against your copies.
-- W3 is planner and wrote the prototype; ask_aar_builders names W4 and W3. The grades are W1's.
-- objective_met is 'in part': written and read back MATCH; C6, C7 (c) and the payload limit not shown; no run since the write; manual entry not written.
-- After the insert: SELECT * FROM ask_aar_snapshots_check(); SELECT * FROM ask_aar_grades_check();
-- The session line below must be the coordinator's own session; written_by is read from it.
BEGIN;
SET LOCAL truth.session_id = '<COORDINATOR SESSION, registered to seat 36>';
WITH s AS (
INSERT INTO ask_aar_snapshots (ask, rev, title, objective, objective_met, objective_met_reason, objective_source, written_by, prior_row, operator_words, card, owner_seat, plan, build_files, revert, grades, md5_written, audit_ids, objects, tests, readbacks, run_evidence, manuals, status, sources)
VALUES (578, '3', $t$ASK 578: the child reads the engine's Shared Library from the call; the child's own copy is removed$t$,
  $t$The child workflow (the second alternate pass) stores its own copy of the Shared Library, equal to the engine's. Every library change is written twice, and a run stops with pkgLIB1 if the two copies differ. Make the engine's copy the only one: the engine sends its library text in the one call it makes to the child, and the child's library readers read it from the call. Expected effect: one library write instead of two; the fault "engine and child libraries differ" can no longer occur; less stored in each child version. It does not make a run faster. No prompt, reasoning setting, model setting, check rule or output changes. (plan rev 3, section 1 OBJECTIVE, fairjudge/w3/a578/ASK578_plan_rev3.md md5 53fe3c1d)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 19:08 CST 2026-11-24 on the operator's press, and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11851, 11852; audit 41852). Engine 634afc23 to 912dd47a, one node changed (Alternate Pass Call sends the field lib); child 85515391 to aad0ad9c, 14 readers and Library Check (ASK 422a) changed, the Shared Library node removed, 155 nodes. IN PART because the plan's DONE asks for the manual entry and two live runs in which the second alternate pass runs, and neither exists. SHOWN: C1 to C5 and C8 on the targets and on the fetch-backs (t578c, 22 checks, ALL PASS; standing set 31 PASS, 0 FAIL; pair check PASSES with the child's Library Check run on what the engine sends); C7 (a) and (b) by a one-time test workflow run on the operator's press (a 1,203,331-character text resolved and arrived whole; Wall 11752, 11753). NOT SHOWN: C6 (the readers' outputs on a real second alternate pass; the inputs cannot be rebuilt from stored rows, Wall 11744); C7 (c) (the real child execution's saved size and duration); the payload limit of the instance is NOT ESTABLISHED (the test call carried 1.2 MB, the real call about 9.1 MB; W1 N2). W1's N1: the pair check matches the Alternate Pass Call expression text and does not evaluate it, so the first live run that reaches the second alternate pass is the proof. Measured: the stored child shrinks from 1,422,386 to 97,905 characters; each child execution now stores the 1.28 MB library text once, about 6.7 percent of the one stored child execution read (42258, 18,981,883 bytes); the engine stores no item that holds the text (Wall 11848). Exception accepted by the grader: the engine's Alternate Pass Call carries no ASK 578 comment, because an n8n expression ends at the first "}}" (W1 N5, Wall 11850). After this write a Library change is made on the engine only.$t$,
  '11148, 11152, 11173, 11174, 11175, 11739, 11740, 11744, 11746, 11749, 11752, 11753, 11837, 11842, 11844, 11846, 11848, 11850, 11851, 11852',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$(1) W3's thread, 19:18 CST 2026-11-23: he pressed "Approve for build" on the card "Approve ASK 578 for build: remove the child's own copy of the Shared Library?" (Wall 11152). (2) W3's thread, 14:04 CST 2026-11-24, verbatim: "Let's take care of the library consolidation with the rest of these updates we're going to do for the lab improvements." (md_notes_rulings row 539; not a write approval). (3) W4's thread, 16:24 CST 2026-11-24: he pressed the card for the one-time C7 test workflow (Wall 11752; the card id and its wording were not read by W3). (4) W4's write card "Write ASK 578 (child reads the engine's library from the call) to live now?": he pressed "Write it" at 19:08 CST 2026-11-24 (W4's thread note to W3; audit 41852 names the card id; W3 did not read the card).$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "question": "Write ASK 578 (child reads the engine's library from the call) to live now?", "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo5889aNhA2t7p2Qxs1AsPXcHz", "press_time": "19:08 CST 2026-11-24", "options": "Write it / Hold", "source": "W4's thread note to W3, 19:09 CST 2026-11-24; audit 41852 (names the card id); Wall 11851. Not read by W3.", "build_card": {"thread": "W3", "question": "Approve ASK 578 for build: remove the child's own copy of the Shared Library?", "answer": "Approve for build", "press_time": "19:18 CST 2026-11-23", "source": "Wall 11152 (W3)"}, "test_card": {"thread": "W4", "what": "run the one-time C7 test workflow", "press_time": "16:24 CST 2026-11-24", "source": "Wall 11752. Card id and wording not read by W3."}}$j$::jsonb,
  'W3',
  $j${"md5": "53fe3c1d", "path": "fairjudge/w3/a578/ASK578_plan_rev3.md", "note": "plan rev 3 by W3, in the ASK FORM; graded PASS WITH N1, N2 by W1 (Wall 11739). Draft 2 (ASK578_plan.md f19c711a, W1 PASS Wall 11148) carried the build approval of 2026-11-23; rev 3 changes the form, the base and how C6 and C7 are shown, not the change.", "commit": "50108126", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11739, 11148"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"md5": "a013260d", "sha256_prefix": "c5bc9fd3", "path": "ask578/w4/b3/target_engine_578.json", "note": "the engine target as written; W4 and W1 name it by the sha256 prefix", "source": "md5sum and sha256sum by W3; Wall 11850"}, {"md5": "568cfab0", "sha256_prefix": "7eb149f4", "path": "ask578/w4/b3/target_child_578.json", "note": "the child target as written (rev 1: the 15 changed child nodes carry an ASK 578 comment). The untagged cut, sha256 bc5b5f08, md5 857b5839, is kept in b3/cut2_untagged/ and was not written.", "source": "md5sum and sha256sum by W3; Wall 11844, 11850"}, {"md5": "82496956", "sha256_prefix": "9700d592", "path": "ask578/w4/b3/notes578.md", "note": "build notes with REV 1; read whole by W3", "commit": "f60f29df", "source": "md5sum and sha256sum by W3; Wall 11844; audit 41852"}, {"md5": "4a12905c", "path": "ask578/w4/b3/t578c.js", "note": "the build and test: W3's t578b.js with two tag strings changed (sha256 prefix 36a02bef, as the notes name it)", "source": "md5sum and sha256sum by W3; notes578.md"}, {"md5": "0c71cc70", "path": "ask578/w4/b3/out_t578c.txt", "note": "test output: 22 lines beginning PASS (counted by W3), then ALL PASS (22 checks)", "source": "md5sum, read and counted by W3"}, {"md5": "6f8feb3a", "path": "ask578/w4/write2/write578.sh", "note": "the write script: refuses on a running execution, a moved node or a failed check; engine first, then child", "source": "md5sum by W3; notes578.md"}, {"md5": "3bbe14d2", "path": "ask578/w4/write2/write578_run.txt", "note": "the write's own output: both PUTs http 200; engine 912dd47a-da89-4cba-9a9b-fb5b6d8f1efa active, 423 nodes, params equal put, connections equal, changed Alternate Pass Call; child aad0ad9c-ecc7-49a1-9079-57a065d9ec74 active, 155 nodes, params equal put, connections equal, changed the 14 readers and Library Check (ASK 422a), Shared Library removed; standing 31 PASS, 0 FAIL before and after; pair: engine lib 027c8c4a71282403 map 771e35cfe3e3b51b, the child's Library Check run on the engine text in the call PASSES", "source": "md5sum and read by W3"}, {"md5": "e23263ff", "sha256_prefix": "3600fafb", "path": "ask578/w4/write2/fetchback_eng_578.json", "note": "engine fetch-back after the write", "source": "md5sum and sha256sum by W3"}, {"md5": "e3fb0d4f", "sha256_prefix": "29b7f676", "path": "ask578/w4/write2/fetchback_child_578.json", "note": "child fetch-back after the write; W3 read the Library Check node and counted 14 nodes that read pass.lib and no Shared Library node in it", "source": "md5sum, sha256sum and read by W3"}, {"md5": "efbc2127", "path": "ask578/w4/c7/out_c7.txt", "note": "the C7 test result (parent execution 42353, child 42354); test files c7_child.json 7392aa01 and c7_parent.json a7df6562 (md5, equal to the names on Wall 11746)", "commit": "8390e6f3", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11746, 11752"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"engine": {"path": "ask578/w4/write2/revert_eng_578.json", "md5": "a105aa58", "note": "the engine before ASK 578 (634afc23), 423 nodes, made at the write"}, "child": {"path": "ask578/w4/write2/revert_child_578.json", "md5": "00d4476b", "note": "the child before ASK 578 (85515391), 156 nodes with its Shared Library node, made at the write"}, "order": "an engine that sends lib with a child that still holds its own node passes (W4's control, notes578.md), so the child can be reverted alone; a 578 child with an engine that does not send lib throws pkgLIB1 at Library Check", "database": "none: no database object was changed", "rehearsed": "no", "source": "md5sum and node counts by W3; audit 41852; Wall 11851; notes578.md"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1, N2 (plan rev 3)", "wall_id": 11739, "md5_graded": "53fe3c1d", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11739; fairjudge/w1/g578/grade_plan578_rev3.md (commit cd27b44e)"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1 (the C7 test workflows, child 7392aa01 and parent a7df6562) and PASS WITH N1 (the C7 result and the availableInMCP deviation)", "wall_id": 11753, "md5_graded": "7392aa01", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11749 (commit 724b9a31), 11753 (commit 38aae6a7)"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "FAIL F1 (re-cut 2, untagged cut: no changed node carried an ASK 578 comment, ASK 599 rule 10); fixed in rev 1", "wall_id": 11842, "md5_graded": "857b5839", "verdict_norm": "FAIL", "source": "Wall 11842; fairjudge/w1/g578/grade_build578_recut2.md (commit 6eb80a6c)"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1 to N5 (re-cut 2 rev 1, engine target: W1's t578c rebuild is byte-equal to engine c5bc9fd3; the md5 here is W3's md5sum of that file)", "wall_id": 11850, "md5_graded": "a013260d", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11850"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1 to N5 (re-cut 2 rev 1, child target: byte-equal to child 7eb149f4; the same grade)", "wall_id": 11850, "md5_graded": "568cfab0", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11850"}]$j$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['a013260d', '568cfab0'], '[41852]'::jsonb,
  $j$[{"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "ORACLE_DEBATE_V1 (engine)", "before": "634afc23", "after": "912dd47a-da89-4cba-9a9b-fb5b6d8f1efa (19:08 CST), active, 423 nodes; one node changed: Alternate Pass Call, whose pass expression also sends lib: $('Shared Library').params.jsCode"}, {"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "child (second alternate pass)", "before": "85515391, 156 nodes", "after": "aad0ad9c-ecc7-49a1-9079-57a065d9ec74, active, 155 nodes; 14 readers read $('Alternate Pass In').first().json.pass.lib; Library Check (ASK 422a) checks the received text against the engine's lib sha and map sha, throws pkgLIB1 otherwise, and drops lib from pass; node Shared Library REMOVED"}, {"kind": "team tools on the shared mount (not n8n)", "name": "standing/lib.cjs and run.cjs (serveFrom); ask557/w4/build/test557.js --pair; ask579/w4/b2/fixhdr579.js", "before": "each expected a child Shared Library node", "after": "a child with no Shared Library node is served the engine's library; the pair check runs the child's Library Check on what the engine sends; fixhdr skips a file with no Library. Put on the mount before W1's grade (W4's stated mistake, W1 N4); before-copies in ask578/w4/b3/."}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"name": "t578c.js on the base (live 634afc23 / 85515391), 22 checks", "result": "ALL PASS by W4 and by W1's own rebuild (byte-equal targets). 14 readers found (the 13 named stubs and R2 Alt Judge Enforcer Retry Build); no other child node names the Shared Library node; for all 14 keys the engine library rebuilds the same text as the child library did; the child asks for 14 keys of 72, served by 3,494 of 3,858 library lines.", "source": "out_t578c.txt 0c71cc70; Wall 11844, 11850"}, {"name": "Standing set and pair check", "result": "31 PASS, 0 FAIL on the targets, at the write and on live (S4: engine 290 of 290 and child 67 of 67 expressions compile). Pair controls: 578 engine with 578 child PASSES; live engine with 578 child THROWS (the engine does not send the text); live pair PASSES; 578 engine with live child PASSES.", "source": "out_standing_578.txt; write578_run.txt 3bbe14d2; notes578.md; Wall 11842, 11850, 11852"}, {"name": "C7 one-time test workflow (parent execution 42353, child 42354), run on the operator's press", "result": "(a) PASS: $('Shared Library').params.jsCode resolved in the Execute Workflow node though the Shared Library node never ran; (b) PASS: the child received 1,203,331 characters, head and tail equal. Both test workflows were never active and were deleted, the deletion read back. Deviation: the parent's settings gained availableInMCP true before the run (W1: an access flag only, accepted). (c) and the payload limit stay owed.", "source": "out_c7.txt efbc2127; Wall 11752, 11753"}, {"name": "Caller search (W1's plan note N1)", "result": "197 workflows read; 24 Execute Workflow nodes; exactly 1 names the child: Alternate Pass Call in the engine.", "source": "Wall 11740"}, {"name": "C6 (readers' outputs on a real second alternate pass)", "result": "NOT SHOWN. The inputs cannot be rebuilt from stored rows (Wall 11744); C1 (byte-equal sources) stands in its place, as the plan allows.", "source": "Wall 11744; plan rev 3 C6"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "result": "MATCH (live engine 912dd47a, 423 nodes, and child aad0ad9c, 155 nodes, equal the graded targets c5bc9fd3 and 7eb149f4 on every node and on connections; against 634afc23 and 85515391 only Alternate Pass Call (engine) and the 14 readers plus Library Check (child) changed, and the child Shared Library is removed; on live: standing 31/0, pair Library Check PASSES, lib 027c8c4a71282403, map 771e35cfe3e3b51b)", "wall_id": 11852, "source": "Wall 11852; fairjudge/w1/g578/readback_578.md (commit 353eb7b0)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"case": "NO RUN YET since the write. A run proves this ASK only if it reaches the second alternate pass.", "runs": [], "mark_for_the_next_run": "in a run that reaches the second alternate pass: the child's Library Check output shows lib422 with same true; the 13 stubs execute, and R2 Alt Judge Enforcer Retry Build when a retry is needed; the pass's rows are stored; no \"pkgLIB\" text in debate_errors. C7 (c), the child execution's saved size and duration, is reported from the first such run. Two such runs are owed.", "not_shown": "the real call (about 9.1 MB) passing on this instance; C6; C7 (c); the try-node re-call path (not shown by run 42071, Wall 11756).", "source": "plan rev 3 section 6; notes578.md; Wall 11842, 11852"}$j$::jsonb,
